Z||000002||Tigger||10-09-2001||04:17 PM||||Sweet!!!!||||reg||14
Z||000003||mrfixit58||10-09-2001||04:31 PM||||Bob,<P>That looks so COOL! Don't know about the orange seat inserts though. Take a look at the 69 Camaro Indy Pace Car interior. It used a LOT of orange and black and I've always thought it was the nicest of all the first generation Camaro interiors. Maybe you can use it for some styling hints. I guess I won't see it at our next meeting. But maybe soon after?<P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||rmorgandotcom||10-09-2001||05:18 PM||||Thats really nice, definitely an eye catcher.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/rmorgandotcom/Fiero/Finale1thumb.jpg"> <BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE> <BR><LI><I>finale body on a86 4 cylinder 5 speed</I><BR><LI><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/rmorgandotcom/" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/rmorgandotcom/</A><BR></UL>||||reg||12
Z||000005||Cozmo||10-09-2001||06:33 PM||||Thanks folks...<BR>It's not easy being orange...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Roy, I'll check into that Indy Camaro for some styling input.  The GT won't be at the meeting tomorrow nite but it should be at the 1st Florida swap meet (Shameless plug follows)... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010086.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010086.html</A> <BR>Tigger, I may do my project car ('87 Coupe, 4.X Caddy conversion) this same orange color combo.<BR>Someone suggested we use green spark plug wires so it would look like a pumpkin...<BR>We beat them mercilessly...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
